{"id": "EUVD-2026-86119", "enisaUuid": "053b512e-71e5-3eef-9c96-3ac424227555", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngfs2: fix quota init duplicate scan\n\ngfs2_quota_init() checks for duplicate quota_change IDs while holding\nqd_lock and the quota hash bucket bitlock. That path used\ngfs2_qd_search_bucket(), which takes a lockref reference via\nlockref_get_not_dead().\n\nOn PREEMPT_RT this may sleep, which is not allowed under the bucket\nbitlock, triggering \"sleeping function called from invalid context\".\n\nUse a no-ref bucket lookup in this path, then continue duplicate\nhandling without taking a lockref there.\n\nRefactor gfs2_qd_search_bucket() to build on top of the no-ref helper\nso lookup traversal stays in one place.\n\nThis patch fixes a bug reported by syzbot.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:05:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T05:30:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7fdcf16e5e14e11028f5bcaa6d25075eb5e876a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/812a766e2b0a8f4d094393fad13475c57f5f86db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b99a1f0f18ee50445907f55069e88bcfd8947383"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97521", "GHSA-jgmg-x8vv-p7hr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "021dab7c-d365-33c6-a50c-74788382bf92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0bda9fe9-7456-332e-ac09-3dd6f6e8b56e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de0d95c26c41c1776e4d23b1a8b3f2bcfd1dae5f <7fdcf16e5e14e11028f5bcaa6d25075eb5e876a0"}, {"id": "1df33e8c-7cca-30ba-98c7-3db6f3dacab9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "2c9b8f56-c523-35f8-9f1f-158e5419224e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de0d95c26c41c1776e4d23b1a8b3f2bcfd1dae5f <812a766e2b0a8f4d094393fad13475c57f5f86db"}, {"id": "3285b2c1-3f16-3bde-b4c8-a91e34c7eb50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de0d95c26c41c1776e4d23b1a8b3f2bcfd1dae5f <b99a1f0f18ee50445907f55069e88bcfd8947383"}, {"id": "3b6a34fd-c0c1-3a89-81e0-4ee657cac9fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "5f795c77-a96d-3da5-a051-00c6bb4faa97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "95236997-837e-3992-a409-15534e860026", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8aca4c5d-8873-388f-b893-2e63cda0172d", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}